# Loose rivet scratch dropped in the repo ROOT (ee2c831: "dist/ and loose
# yaml"). These MUST stay anchored with a leading `/`: unanchored, git matches
# the basename at any depth, so `tools/fixtures/*/requirements.yaml` was
# silently excluded — `git add <dir>` skips it and still exits 0. The tracked
# artifacts/ and safety/stpa/ copies were unaffected only because gitignore
# does not apply to already-tracked files.
/architecture.yaml
/requirements.yaml
/verification.yaml

# Stale dev artifacts — re-add explicitly if needed.
/dashboard-render*.png

# LP solver problem dumps written into the repo root by HiGHS/good_lp
# during network-calculus (PLP/TFA) test runs — regenerable scratch.
*.lp

# cargo-mutants output — regenerable mutation-testing scratch.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Python bytecode cache from tools/*.py — regenerable.
__pycache__/

# Agent-maintained durable session scratch — never commit.
.pulseengine-session-notes.md

# fixture-vm build products. The qcow2 is a full NixOS disk image (hundreds of
# MB) that the trace-fixtures workflow copies out of the container's nix store;
# `result` is nix's default out-link. Both are regenerable, and neither has ever
# been ignored — which stayed harmless only because the build had never once got
# far enough to produce either one.
/tools/fixture-vm/nixos.qcow2
/tools/fixture-vm/result

# Nested-workspace build output. `/target` above is ROOT-ANCHORED, so it does
# not cover the three sibling workspaces; before the clippy-scope guardrail
# (REQ-GUARD-GATE-EVIDENCE-002 g) nothing routinely built in them, so the gap
# never showed. It does now — running clippy repo-wide leaves untracked
# `target/` in each, and untracked noise hides real changes.
codegen-exec-oracle/target/
codegen-kiln-oracle/target/
fuzz/target/
